          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "7e86764a-353e-4b9a-9c2b-0aeaeabedf63"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "306c2d70-d7a0-4134-bb40-4d841072b4a5"
        }
      ],
      "level": 1,
      "text": "Other number bases: octal and base 4"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "e57eac43-6bee-550b-8e01-6ac56388ec47",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "7e86764a-353e-4b9a-9c2b-0aeaeabedf63"
        },
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "306c2d70-d7a0-4134-bb40-4d841072b4a5"
        }
      ],
      "text": "Group bits because these bases are powers of two.\n\n- Base 4: 2 bits per digit.\n- Base 8: 3 bits per digit.\n- Base 16: 4 bits per digit; A–F mean decimal 10–15.\n\nStart each grouping at the radix point and work outward. Pad the far left of an integer or far right of a fraction with zeroes."
    },
    {
      "type": "worked_example",
      "id": "25ca7ba3-4a01-5f0c-a6d6-6632275ca62e",
      "citations": [
        {
          "source_id": "ff6535b5-436e-42d5-8e1e-da0e01122696",
          "version": 1,
          "chunk_id": "306c2d70-d7a0-4134-bb40-4d841072b4a5"
        }
      ],
      "title": "One pattern, two compact forms",
      "prompt": "Convert $(10110110)_2$ to hex and octal.",
      "steps": [
        {
          "explanation": "Group by four for hex.",
          "latex": "1011\\;0110\\Rightarrow(\\mathrm{B6})_{16}"
        },
        {
          "explanation": "Group by three for octal, padding only at the far left.",
          "latex": "010\\;110\\;110\\Rightarrow(266)_8"
        },
        {
          "explanation": "Check the value independently.",
          "latex": "2(8^2)+6(8)+6=182"
        }
      ],
      "answer": "$(\\mathrm{B6})_{16}=(266)_8=182$. Slide 43 prints 226 in its octal result; the grouping gives 266."
    },
    {
      "type": "worked_example",
      "id": "e66690c3-d12f-5528-91c0-10f4677bfb85",
      "citations": [
        {
